From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaydens-tasty-slop
 <325336397+jaydens-tasty-slop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:13:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: samsung-ams968hh01: add brightness control

The driver only runs the panel at its top luminance step, 360 cd/m2.
Register a backlight device and send the vendor brightness update for
each of its 256 levels: AID (register 0x90), ELVSS, CAPS and the gamma
table of the level's luminance step, then the gamma update key, in HS
mode on the first link as the vendor driver does. Init sends the current
level, so the panel comes up at it; level 255 sends the same bytes as
before.

The 256 levels map onto 65 luminance steps from 2 to 360 cd/m2. The
gamma table of each step below 360 cd/m2 is computed from the panel's
MTP offsets as the vendor "smart dimming" code does: the offsets give
the voltages of the gamma points on the calibrated 360 cd/m2 curve, each
point of a step takes the gray level whose luminance on that curve is
nearest the step's target, and the table encodes those levels' voltages.
The step tables and luminance curves come from the vendor driver and
device tree in Samsung's GPL-2.0 kernel source for the SM-T820
(drivers/video/msm/mdss/samsung/ANA38401_AMS968HH01/ and
ss_dsi_smart_dimming_common.c). The computation is written here as plain
linear interpolation and clamping, which gives the same tables.

The stock kernel prints every table it computes
(/sys/devices/virtual/lcd/panel/aid_log). For the MTP bytes of an
SM-T820 panel, this code, built on the host, gives the same 65 tables.

ACL and HBM are not implemented; ACL stays off as before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
